      "created_at": "2015-04-25T17:27:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This came up in the last game we'd played, and it's about how turn-based cards work</p><p>Nightmist had her Amulet of the Elder gods out,which has a \"the first time Nightmist would be dealt damage each turn, you may discard 2 cards. if you do, you may redirect that damage to a target of your choice.\"</p><p>i could swear there's another example or so, but the question here is: does that mean during her turn, another hero's turn, enviroment's turn, and villain's turn are all subject to, if enough cards exist in her hand, to have all damage thrown around? or are turns(in this instance) given by environment/villain/hero?</p><p>any clarification is greatly appreciated</p><p>muchly thanks folks :)</p>",
